description: Keep code files under 300 LOC (comments/blanks ignored); split when larger
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code file size limit

- Code files must not exceed **300 lines of code**.
- **Counting:** only non-empty, non-comment lines count. Blank lines and comments (including block comments and JSDoc) are ignored.
- Applies to source code (e.g. `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.mjs`, `.cjs`, `.css`, `.scss`, `.sql` in `src/` and similar). Does not apply to generated output, lockfiles, data dumps, or vendored code.
- When adding or editing code would push a file over 300 lines of code, **split** it first: extract modules, helpers, route handlers, queries, or components into new files.
- Prefer cohesive splits (one concern per file) over dumping leftovers into a catch-all.
- Do not grow an already oversized file; when touching one, extract enough that the result stays ≤ 300 lines of code (or clearly shrinks toward that limit).

